    864  f102							; +1 line/frame). Rows 0/1 now store+WSYNC before the tide block, then
    865  f102							; jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line = 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC
    866  f102							; = 72 <=76). Row2 path byte-identical in cost (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    867  f102							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    868  f102							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
    869  f102							; A1 gap fix (2026-10-05): `sta Temp` (+3c in .Row) pushed gaps to
    870  f102							; 77/79 = stall EVERY frame (265-line frames). `sta LineCount` moved
    871  f102							; AFTER `sta WSYNC` — same bytes, -3c from the gap window, +3c to the
    872  f102							; first body line (66max+3LC[+3jmp]+3WSYNC = 75 rows0/1, 72 row2).
    873  f102							; LineCount is not read until the line's `dec` tail — the early store
    874  f102							; was never required; keep the store strictly between WSYNC and .Line.
