    890  f115							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    891  f115							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    892  f115							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    893  f115							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    894  f115							; CORRECTED 2026-10-22 (Phase 4): that "line S+1" is only true for a
    895  f115							; sprite whose pixels come AFTER the store. Per Stella's Player::grp /
    896  f115							; updatePattern, a GRP write lands in myPatternNew and renders at once, so
    897  f115							; the boundary is the sprite's own pixel start (cycle ~(61+X)/3). With
    898  f115							; VDELP0=1 (set in the VBL, see the comment there) the live pattern is
    899  f115							; `myPatternOld`, latched by the GRP1 store at c58, so P0 is correct for
    900  f115							; every X < 113 px and its art row r sits on the SAME scanline as
    901  f115							; PlayerColTable[r] (COLUP0 lands at c19, before all pixels) — i.e. the
    902  f115							; art and its per-row colours finally agree. Do not reorder the colour
    903  f115							; path behind the graphics: COLUP0 must stay the first store in the body.
    904  f115							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    905  f115							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    906  f115							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    907  f115							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    908  f115							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    909  f115							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    910  f115							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    911  f115							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    912  f115							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    913  f115							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    914  f115							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    915  f115							; (PlayerColTable [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    916  f115							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    917  f115							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    918  f115							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    919  f115							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    920  f115							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    921  f115							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    922  f115							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    923  f115							; ObjSprites+107 must stay in ONE page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    924  f115							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    925  f115							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and PlayerColTable in $F8xx
    926  f115							; (verify_build guards the A0=10 page-cross budget).
    927  f115							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    928  f115							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    929  f115							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    930  f115							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    931  f115							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    932  f115							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    933  f115							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
    934  f115							; Keep the hot path at <= 70c work: an overrun duplicates the scanline.
    935  f115		       c0 0b		      cpy	#PLAYER_SPRITE_H - 1
    936  f117		       b0 3d		      bcs	.GrpSkip	; A0 >= 11 (incl $ff): no color/beam this line.
    937  f119							; A0=11 skips too (Class-A stall line): rows
    938  f119							; 10/11 share color+beam bytes, so row 10's
    939  f119							; writes are still in effect here.
    940  f119							; --- Laser S2.2: ENAM0 = PlayerColTable bit1 & LaserState.b1 ----------
    941  f119							; Phase 0 (2026-10-21): the retired BeamMask table duplicated bit 1 of
    942  f119							; PlayerColTable for a separate 4c fetch. One yellow strip on RoomY+2
    943  f119							; only (user directive 2026-10-08: the red row-3 strip is gone; the kill
    944  f119							; window in LaserHitTestBody keeps rows RoomY+2..3 = superset of the
    945  f119							; draw). In-window path only (Y<=11), so outside the window ENAM0 keeps
    946  f119							; its last write ($00 at A0=10) — no HUD artifact. verify_build asserts
