   2683  f980							; --- Cell walk (cell_collision_plan 2.1): test the PF buffers directly ---
   2684  f980							; The ZP rect cache ($CC-$DF, 5-slot limit) is gone from THIS walker: the
   2685  f980							; render buffers PF0/1/2Buf ARE the map (BombMarkWalls punches bomb holes
   2686  f980							; into them), so room complexity is unbounded and geometry parity is proven
   2687  f980							; by tools/test_cell_map.py (box vs geometry, all models/rooms).
   2688  f980							; Prologue ranges (all left-half space): CollisionCellY = top row,
   2689  f980							; CollisionEndY = bottom row, CollisionEndX = min col, CollisionCellX = max
   2690  f980							; col — cols are endpoint-mirrored above, so ALWAYS 0-19 here (no in-loop
   2691  f980							; mirror; bank2 display-space walkers add their own when they convert).
   2692  f980							; RectCount = running row, CollisionX = running col (both were walk temps
   2693  f980							; before — same ZP, no new allocation).
   2694  f980							; Exits: HIT -> jmp HotOverlapFlag (tail, C=1 contract preserved);
   2695  f980							;	  miss -> clc / rts. Stack depth during the walk = old walk exactly
   2696  f980							;	  (no jsr added — sim_bomb_fuse gameplay min-SP guard stays $F8).
